# comptime_reflect.tkr — the §14 B4 ACCEPT host: Family-B comptime TYPE reflection (Extent-1). A
# `@sizeof<T>()` / `@typename<T>()` call binds its type argument to the comptime's type parameter, the
# body's `T.size` / `T.name` reflection is resolved over that concrete type before the body is typed, and
# the call is folded to the literal slot-size / rendered-name. Each scenario names itself and asserts its
# announced value through `run`/`run_str` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself.

Feature: comptime_reflect — Family-B comptime type reflection (§14 B4)

  Scenario: comptime_sizeof_i32 — @sizeof<i32>() folds T.size over i32 to 4
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_sizeof_i32: ok"

  Scenario: comptime_sizeof_bool — @sizeof<bool>() folds T.size over bool to 1
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_sizeof_bool: ok"

  Scenario: comptime_typename_i32 — @typename<i32>() folds T.name over i32 to "i32"
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_typename_i32: ok"
